==English==
{{wp}}
[[Image:Leuciscus leuciscus Hungary.jpg|thumb|right|200px|{{vern|common dace}} (''[[Leuciscus leuciscus]]'']]

===Etymology===
Old variant of earlier {{nrhot|en|darse|notext=1}}, from Late {{inh|en|enm|darse}} (also as {{m|enm|dace}} already), from {{der|en|fro|darz}}, {{lg|oblique}} {{lg|plural}} form of {{m|fro|dart||spear; javelin}}.<br/>
For a similar loss of ''r'', compare {{m|en|bass}}, while for the pronunciation with {{IPAchar|/eɪ/}}, see {{m|en|scarce}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/deɪs/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dace.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪs|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|*|s}}

# A [[shoal]]-forming fish of species {{taxfmt|Leuciscus leuciscus|species}}, common to swift rivers in [[England]] and [[Wales]] and in Europe.
#* {{RQ:1984| section=Part One, Chapter 3| passage=Somewhere near at hand, though out of sight, there was a clear, slow-moving stream where '''dace''' were swimming in the pools under the willow trees.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} Any of various related small fish of the family {{taxfmt|Cyprinidae|family}} that live in [[freshwater]] and are native to [[North America]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|dare}}, {{l|en|dart}}

